nts -n astronomy-shop` to see if `jaeger-out` was supposed to be there. The response didn't mention `jaeger-out`, so it's likely that the service is missing or there's a misconfiguration.\n\nNow, the user is in the thinking stage again. They need to decide which tool to use next. The available tools include `exec_kubectl_cmd_safely`, which can run kubectl commands. The next logical step is to check if there's a deployment or pod named `jaeger-out` that's not listed. Since the service isn't present, maybe the deployment is missing. Alternatively, the application might be incorrectly referencing `jaeger-out` instead of `jaeger`.\n\nThe user should check for any pods related to `jaeger-out` to confirm if they're running. If there are no pods, that indicates the service isn't properly deployed. Alternatively, if the service is supposed to be there but isn't, they might need to create it. But since the user is in the mitigation phase, they need to confirm the absence and then take corrective action. \n\nSo, the next tool call should be to check the pods in the namespace to see if `jaeger-out` is running. If not, that confirms the service is missing. Then, they can proceed to either create the service or adjust the application's configuration to use the correct service name.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ab7dfb9892bcac87', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 449, 'prompt_tokens': 4859, 'total_tokens': 5308, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdae-158c-7133-90c2-dfe81fa338b9-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 