eck for any errors in the command. \n\nAlso, after updating the environment variable, they should wait a moment for the pods to restart and then check again. If the issue persists, maybe there\'s another misconfiguration or a different service that\'s causing the problem. But based on the current info, the main issue is the incorrect endpoint in the frontend\'s environment variables.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely  \ntool description: This tool will execute a `kubectl` command to force an update of the `frontend` Deployment and verify the corrected `PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT` value. If the previous `apply` command failed, this will ensure the change is applied and validated.  \n\n**Reasoning:**  \nThe previous `kubectl apply` attempt did not update the environment variable, as the value remained `http://localhost:8080/otlp-http/v1/traces`. This suggests the YAML patch might not have been applied correctly. By explicitly reapplying the updated configuration and verifying the value, we ensure the fix is implemented.  \n\n**Next step:**  \nReapply the corrected configuration and validate the environment variable.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: frontend\\n  namespace: astronomy-shop\\nspec:\\n  template:\\n    spec:\\n      containers:\\n      - name: frontend\\n        env:\\n        - name: PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT\\n          value: http://jaeger.observe.svc.cluster.local/otlp-http/v1/traces\\nEOF"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 673, 'prompt_tokens': 8196, 'total_tokens': 8869, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, 