is using. If the variable is set there, updating the ConfigMap would be necessary. Alternatively, if the deployment is using envFrom, they need to ensure that the ConfigMap/Secret is correctly updated. \n\nBut given the tools available, the user can't directly edit ConfigMaps unless they use kubectl set env or apply. Since that's not working, maybe the issue is with the service resolution. They should check if otel-collector.observe.svc.cluster.local is resolvable. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the application is using a different port or path. The correct endpoint for OTLP is usually http://<collector>:4317/v1/traces. So ensuring the port and path are correct is important. \n\nIn the end, after multiple attempts to update the environment variable without success, the user might need to check the ConfigMap or Secret, or verify the service's DNS resolution. But with the current tools, the best option is to confirm the environment variable's value in the running pod again, ensuring no typos or caching issues. If that fails, the problem might be deeper, like a misconfigured service or a different configuration source.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl exec -n astronomy-shop frontend-65c7cd5577-vstck -- printenv PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a226c10d06e4b55b', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 777, 'prompt_tokens': 12013, 'total_tokens': 12790, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdc0-4975-72f2-a2d3-5e59111132a3-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl exec -n astronomy-shop frontend-65c7cd5577-vstck -- printenv PUBLIC_OTEL_EX