        value: http://$(OTEL_COLLECTOR_NAME):4317\n        - name: WEB_OTEL_SERVICE_NAME\n          value: frontend-web\n        - name: PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT\n          value: http://localhost:8080/otlp-http/v1/traces\n        image: ghcr.io/open-telemetry/demo:2.2.0-frontend\n        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent\n        name: frontend\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 8080\n          name: service\n          protocol: TCP\n        resources:\n          limits:\n            memory: 250Mi\n        securityContext:\n          runAsGroup: 1001\n          runAsNonRoot: true\n          runAsUser: 1001\n        terminationMessagePath: /dev/termination-log\n        terminationMessagePolicy: File\n      dnsPolicy: ClusterFirst\n      restartPolicy: Always\n      schedulerName: default-scheduler\n      securityContext: {}\n      serviceAccount: astronomy-shop\n      serviceAccountName: astronomy-shop\n      terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30\nstatus:\n  availableReplicas: 1\n  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T21:18:15Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T21:18:15Z"\n    message: Deployment has minimum availability.\n    reason: MinimumReplicasAvailable\n    status: "True"\n    type: Available\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T21:17:36Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T21:18:15Z"\n    message: ReplicaSet "frontend-65c7cd5577" has successfully progressed.\n    reason: NewReplicaSetAvailable\n    status: "True"\n    type: Progressing\n  observedGeneration: 1\n  readyReplicas: 1\n  replicas: 1\n  updatedReplicas: 1\n', id='ba55e223-a6ab-4afe-a4ea-243da71fb85c', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-b07c9174519a5c20'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='5a0c2918-2270-4a1f-a662-36b2858603cf'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to fix the issue where the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop is having problems with Jaeger services not resolving. The main error is a NameResolutionError for jaeger-out.observe.svc.cluster.local. \n\nFirst, I checked the services in the namespace and found that jaeger-out isn\'t listed. The jaeger service exists but is an ExternalName pointing to otel-collector.observe.svc.cluster.local. Then, looking at the pods, all services are running, but the application is trying to connect to jaeger-out, which doesn\'t exist.\n\nNext, I checked the frontend pod\'s environment variables and saw that the PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT is set to http://localhost:8080/otlp-http/v1/traces. That\'s incorrect because it\'s using localhost instead of the correct service name. The Deployment YAML confirms this configuration.\n\nSo the root cause is that the frontend service is misconfigured to use localhost for the trace endpoint instead of the jaeger service. The solution is to update the PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT in the frontend Deployment to point to the correct jaeger service, which is jaeger.observe.svc.cluster.local or the ExternalName otel-collector.observe.svc.cluster.local.\n\nNow, I need to modify the Deployment\'s environment variable to fix this. Using the exec_kubectl_cmd_safely tool, I can edit the Deployment\'s YAML to correct the endpoint. After making the change, I should apply the updated configuration and verify that the service can resolve jaeger correctly. Once that\'s done, the tracing should work as expected, and the faults should be mitigated.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely  \ntool description: This tool will execute a `kubectl` command to update the `frontend` Deployment\'s environment variable `PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT` to use the correct Jaeger service endpoint (`jaeger.observe.svc.cluster.local` instead of `localhost`). This will fix the misconfiguration causing the NameResolutionError.  \n\n**Reasoning:**  \nThe `frontend` Deployment\'s `PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT` is incorrectly set to `http://localhost:8080/otlp-http/v1/traces`, which resolves to the pod\'s own IP and fails to connect to Jaeger. The correct endpoint should reference the `jaeger` service (or its ExternalName `otel-collector.observe.svc.cluster.local`). Updating this environment variable will ensure the application sends traces to the correct Jaeger service.  \n\n**Next step:**  \nEdit the `frontend` Deployment\'s YAML to fix the trace endpoint configuration.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: frontend\\n  namespace: astronomy-shop\\nspec:\\n  template:\\n    spec:\\n      containers:\\n      - name: frontend\\n        env:\\n        - name: PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT\\n          value: http://jaeger.observe.svc.cluster.local/otlp-http/v1/traces\\nEOF"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 674, 'prompt_tokens': 7728, 'total_tokens': 8402, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdaf-2642-75c0-9ec2-4d166e479265-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7728, 'output_tokens': 674, 'total_tokens': 8402}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='00118548-3b2e-49d2-9b6e-28a00beab61b'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me go through the steps again to make sure everything is correct. The user had an issue where the Jaeger service wasn't resolving, leading to errors. They checked the services and found that `jaeger-out` wasn't present, but `jaeger` was there as an ExternalName pointing to `otel-collector.observe.svc.cluster.local`.\n\nThe problem was in the `frontend` Deployment's environment variable `PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT`, which was set to `http://localhost:8080/otlp-http/v1/traces`. This was causing the application to try to connect to localhost instead of the correct Jaeger service. \n\nSo, the solution was to update that environment variable to use `jaeger.observe.svc.cluster.local` instead. The user applied the change using `kubectl apply` with a YAML patch. Now, they need to verify if the change was successful. \n\nThe next step is to check the updated Deployment to ensure the environment variable was correctly modified. Then, they should confirm that the service is now resolving properly and that traces are being sent to Jaeger. If everything is fixed, they can submit the result. If not, they might need to check the service configuration again or look into other potential misconfigurations.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployment frontend -n astronomy-shop -o jsonpath=\'{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].env[?(@.name==\\"PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT\\")].value}\'"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9ba17a9917f2d5fe', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 334, 'prompt_tokens': 9077, 'total_tokens': 9411, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdaf-4743-77e3-8ee1-eaf44d3bf81c-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployment frontend -n astronomy-shop -o jsonpath=\'{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].env[?(@.name=="PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT")].value}\''}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9ba17a9