.\n\nSince the environment variable isn\'t updating, maybe the deployment needs to be force-restarted or the ConfigMap/Secret that contains the trace endpoint needs to be updated and rolled out. The user should also confirm that the `jaeger` service is correctly pointing to the `otel-collector` and that the `otel-collector` is functioning as expected.\n</think>\n\nThe environment variable `PUBLIC_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT` in the `frontend` pod is still set to the incorrect value (`http://localhost:8080/otlp-http/v1/traces`), despite multiple attempts to update it. This indicates a persistent misconfiguration or caching issue. The root cause is likely that the application is hardcoded to use `localhost` instead of the correct Jaeger/OTEL Collector endpoint (`jaeger.observe.svc.cluster.local` or `otel-collector.observe.svc.cluster.local`). \n\n**Final Action:**  \nForce a restart of the `frontend` Deployment to ensure the updated configuration takes effect. If the issue persists, verify the `otel-collector` service\'s health and network policies.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl rollout restart deployment/frontend -n astronomy-shop"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=669, prompt_tokens=13098, total_tokens=13767, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdc2-6a44-77d0-be9a-08c6802be00a-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 13098, 'output_tokens': 669, 'total_tokens': 13767}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='18259067-3125-4579-b69f-6f587561e552')]]
